From: Yusuf İhsan KILINÇ
Subject: [PATCH 0086] anv: RT, allocate the ray query BO and the BTD FIFO and emit 3DSTATE_BTD on first use

On top of 0085 (src/mesa-rt: a3ad934 + the 935ef655 diff + 0085). Replaces 0085's device-creation decision
(anv_device_uses_btd: "the device enabled KHR_ray_query or KHR_ray_tracing_pipeline") with a first-use one.
Only has an effect with -Dintel-rt=enabled (ANV_SUPPORT_RT=1); with intel-rt=disabled anv_device_has_rt_hw()
is constant false and btd_fifo_bo stays NULL, so nothing changes. Built in src/mesa-rt/build-rtopt; NOT installed.
Generated-by: LLM

Why: a Vulkan app (here the Metal plugin, which runs in every Metal process including WindowServer) enables
VK_KHR_ray_query whenever the device has it, because it cannot know at vkCreateDevice whether the process will
ever trace a ray. With ANV that costs every such device, at creation:
  - "ray queries" BO: max_scratch_ids[COMPUTE] * 32 * BRW_RT_SIZEOF_RAY_QUERY (256 B)
    = 128 * DSS bound * 32 * 256 B, 20 MiB on 20 DSS (B580),
  - "rt-btd-fifo" BO: 128 KiB per DSS, 2.5 MiB on 20 DSS,
  - 3DSTATE_BTD in every queue's initial state.
The rest already is first-use in upstream: the ray query shadow BOs and the RT scratch BOs (allocated while
recording, published with p_atomic_cmpxchg), the "bvh build" BO pool (no BO until a build), the BVH meta
pipelines (first build). This does the same for the three above, as Intel's compute runtime (NEO) does for
its ray tracing buffers and 3DSTATE_BTD (allocated / programmed for the first kernel that uses ray tracing):
  - anv_device_get_rt_bo(): the shadow-BO pattern for ray_query_bo[idx] and btd_fifo_bo.
  - anv_cmd_buffer_use_rt_hw(): called where a command buffer binds a shader with ray queries
    (anv_cmd_buffer_set_rt_query_buffer: compute, graphics and RT stages) and where it flushes a ray
    tracing pipeline (cmd_buffer_flush_rt_state, which already emits its own 3DSTATE_BTD per command
    buffer); allocates the FIFO and sets anv_cmd_state::uses_rt_hw (ORed into the primary by
    vkCmdExecuteCommands).
  - genX(queue_init_rt_state)(): at submission (device mutex held), the first time a queue gets a command
    buffer with uses_rt_hw, an async batch on that queue's context with the same 3DSTATE_BTD the initial
    state used to carry (CS stall first: non-pipelined state on a context that already ran work; no
    PIPELINE_SELECT: 3DSTATE_BTD is render|compute and Xe2 has none). It runs before the submission's
    command buffers (same exec queue, submitted first). Freed like init_submit.
  - init_common_queue_state(): emits 3DSTATE_BTD only when the FIFO exists, i.e. a context created after
    the device used RT (anv_nvmtl_recover.c replacing a banned exec queue) gets it with its initial
    state; queue->rt_state_initialized follows. The recovery drops rt_init_submit with the init submits.
A device that enables the RT extensions and never records RT work keeps exactly the BOs and context state
of a device without them (and of the intel-rt=disabled build); a device that uses ray queries gets the
same 3DSTATE_BTD and BOs as before, one submission later instead of at creation.
device_has_compute_queue (only used for the Wa_14022863161 second ray query BO) goes away: ray_query_bo[1]
is now allocated by the first compute-queue command buffer that needs it.

